  "what": "How many painted frames the drawer's chrome can occupy on the conversation being entered, and how much the layout moves while it is there. ONE READING, NOT A CONSTANT (design/QA round 1, Q4): the close waits for the NEW conversation's frame to land, so the count is a function of how fast that read answers on the machine and under the load it ran on - 4 frames at fleet load ~30, 8 at load ~58. While that frame is in flight the drawer reads UNREAD (the bar carries NO clause; the body reads `Reading the asks\u2026`) and must not close, because a switch to a conversation that DOES have asks is indistinguishable for exactly that interval.",
